-- title:
--   A height homomorphism GL₂(ℚᵣ)→ℤ from quaternionic endomorphisms
-- statement:
--   Let $r$ be a prime, $K$ a field of characteristic $r$, and $\Phi$ a `FormalODModule` over $K$ for $r$: a two-dimensional commutative formal group law $F$ over $K$ together with series $\mathrm{act}(a)$, for $a$ in `Zp2 r`, and $\varpi$, each an endomorphism of the law, satisfying $\mathrm{act}(1)=\mathrm{id}$, $\mathrm{act}(ab)=\mathrm{act}(a)\circ\mathrm{act}(b)$, additivity of $a\mapsto\mathrm{act}(a)$ with respect to $F$, $\varpi\circ\varpi=\mathrm{act}(r)$ and $\varpi\circ\mathrm{act}(a)=\mathrm{act}(\sigma a)\circ\varpi$ with $\sigma$ the Witt-vector Frobenius. Assume `Φ.HasHeight 4`, i.e. the series $\mathrm{act}(r)$ has `HasKernelOfDegree` equal to $r^4$. Let $E$ be a ring homomorphism from the centralizer subring of $\{\Phi.\mathrm{actEnd}\,a\}_a\cup\{\Phi.\mathrm{varpiEnd}\}$ in $\mathrm{End}(F)$ to $M_2(\mathbb{Q}_r)$, assumed injective and commensurable with $M_2(\mathbb{Z}_r)$ in the sense that for some $m\in\mathbb{N}$ every $r^m A$ with $A\in M_2(\mathbb{Z}_r)$ lies in the image of $E$, and $r^m E(e)$ has entries in $\mathbb{Z}_r$ for every $e$. Then there is a monoid homomorphism $\nu:\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_r)\to\mathbb{Z}$ (written multiplicatively) such that $\nu(g)=4$ whenever the matrix of $g$ is $r\cdot 1$, and such that for every $e$ in that centralizer and every $g$ with matrix $E(e)$ there is $h\in\mathbb{N}$ with $\nu(g)=h$, the quotient of $K[[X_1,X_2]]$ by the ideal generated by the two components of $e$ finite over $K$, and, for every field $\kappa$ and ring homomorphism $f:K\to\kappa$, the corresponding quotient of $\kappa[[X_1,X_2]]$ by the images of those components of $\kappa$-dimension exactly $r^h$.
--
--   This produces the height homomorphism through which $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_r)$ acts on Drinfeld's functor of rigidified special formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-modules: endomorphisms with invertible coordinate matrix are isogenies whose height is read off from $\nu$, normalised by $\nu(r)=4$. It feeds the computations of kernel degrees and determinants for special formal modules, and the construction of isogenies of height divisible by $4$ over algebraically closed fields.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_FormalODModule_exists_monoidHom_generalLinearGroup_finrank_kerAlgebra_eq_pow_of_hasHeight.lean

